<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:md="using:CircuitRF.Ui.Markdown"
             x:Class="CircuitRF.Ui.Views.Content.MarkdownDocumentView"
             x:DataType="md:MarkdownDocument"
             Background="{DynamicResource SystemChromeLowColor}">

  <!--
    A read-only Markdown document — a workspace's README.md, opened instead of the Welcome tab.

    ONE SelectableTextBlock, not a control per line, for the Release Notes dialog's own reason: a
    selection cannot cross two controls, and somebody reading an example's README wants to copy a
    netlist line or a measurement expression out of it. Bold, italics, bullets, headings and the
    flattened tables are therefore inlines within it (SmallMarkdown parses; MarkdownInlines builds
    the runs).

    MaxWidth, not Stretch: a README read across a maximised window is a line length nobody can follow
    back to the start of. The block is centred in whatever is left.

    There is no edit affordance anywhere in here, which is the whole of how this document is
    read-only — see MarkdownDocument.

    LineSpacing, not LineHeight: a fixed LineHeight holds a line with a picture in it to that height,
    and the picture is then drawn upward over the lines above it. Spacing ADDS to each line's own
    height, so a text line keeps the old 20 px pitch and a picture's line is as tall as the picture.
  -->

  <ScrollViewer Name="BodyScroll"
                Padding="0"
                HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
    <SelectableTextBlock Name="BodyText"
                         TextWrapping="Wrap"
                         FontSize="13"
                         LineSpacing="4"
                         MaxWidth="820"
                         Margin="28,24,28,32"
                         HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                         VerticalAlignment="Top"
                         Foreground="{DynamicResource SystemBaseHighColor}"/>
  </ScrollViewer>

</UserControl>
